---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getBusiness } from '../../lib/content';

const business = await getBusiness();
const locale = 'en';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — EazyFix"
  description="EazyFix Privacy Policy: what data we collect, why, who we share it with and your rights under the GDPR."
  locale={locale}
  business={business}
>
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller of your personal data is <strong>Georgios Tsouchnikas</strong>, a sole proprietor
    trading as <strong>EazyFix</strong>, based in Salamina, Greece, VAT number <strong>160020860</strong>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Privacy email: <a href="mailto:g.touhnikas@gmail.com">g.touhnikas@gmail.com</a></li>
    <li>General email: <a href="mailto:info@eazyfix.gr">info@eazyfix.gr</a></li>
    <li>Phone: <a href="tel:6971234567">6971234567</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details you provide:</strong> name, phone, email, the service you are interested in and your message.</li>
    <li><strong>Contract and billing details:</strong> when you commission work, the details needed for the quote, contract and invoice (e.g. business name, address, VAT number). We do not store card details; payments are handled by a third-party payment provider.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser/device type and security logs generated by the hosting provider.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies and local storage:</strong> see the <a href="/en/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How we collect data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> when you press “Send”, WhatsApp opens with a pre-filled message. Your details are transmitted via WhatsApp (Meta) when you press send there. The website does not store the form data on its own server.</li>
    <li><strong>Email and phone:</strong> when you contact us directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Browsing the website:</strong> technical logs and security data from the hosting provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Responding to enquiries and preparing quotes:</strong> Article 6(1)(b) GDPR (pre-contractual steps) or 6(1)(f) (legitimate interest).</li>
    <li><strong>Performing contracts and invoicing:</strong> Article 6(1)(b) and 6(1)(c) GDPR (legal obligation).</li>
    <li><strong>Website security and operation:</strong> Article 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest).</li>
    <li><strong>Optional communications/consent:</strong> Article 6(1)(a) GDPR where explicitly requested.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>Where necessary for the service, data may be shared with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, CDN and website security.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — source code hosting and public game demos.</li>
    <li><strong>Bunny Fonts</strong> — font delivery from EU infrastructure.</li>
    <li><strong>Meta / WhatsApp</strong> — message transmission when you choose WhatsApp.</li>
    <li><strong>Email provider (Google/Gmail)</strong> — email management.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing, if an online shop is activated.</li>
    <li><strong>Accountant and tax authorities</strong> — where required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data and do not use it for advertising profiling.</p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some providers may process data outside the EU/EEA. In such cases, appropriate GDPR safeguards
    are used (Standard Contractual Clauses and, where applicable, the EU-US Data Privacy Framework).
  </p>

  <h2>7. Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries:</strong> up to 12 months after the last communication.</li>
    <li><strong>Contracts and invoices:</strong> as required by tax and commercial law (typically 5–10 years).</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> for the period set by the hosting provider for security purposes.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> see the <a href="/en/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing, object, data portability and withdraw any consent. You can exercise your rights by emailing <a href="mailto:g.touhnikas@gmail.com">g.touhnikas@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  <p>
    If you believe the processing infringes the GDPR, you may lodge a complaint with the
    <strong>Hellenic Data Protection Authority (HDPA)</strong>,
    1–3 Kifisias Ave., 115 23 Athens, <a href="https://www.dpa.gr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.dpa.gr</a>,
    tel. +30 210 6475600.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    The website uses HTTPS encryption. Access to management systems is restricted and protected by a
    password and a session cookie. Reasonable technical and organisational measures are taken to protect data.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Minors</h2>
  <p>Our services are aimed at adults and professionals. We do not knowingly collect data from minors under 15.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>This policy may be updated. The last updated date is shown at the top of the page.</p>
</LegalLayout>
